    "body": "I think it would make sense to have more consistency between the handling of blobs and img elements (described above). Currently, with an img, when we encounter a file that is decodable but does not represent bitmap media, an InvalidStateError is thrown. Suggestion: perhaps we should separate these two cases: unsupported media type (e.g. vector graphics) -> InvalidStateError; undecodable media -> EncodingError\n",
