    "body": "In the section \"If <var>image</var> is an <code>img</code> element\", should we have something equivalent to this? Example:  If the img is in the broken state (data-x=\"img-error\"), the promise should be rejected with an <code>EncodingError</code> exception. \n\nRight now, the the broken state case gets handled by a catch-all clause for handling imgs that are not in the completely available state. It rejects with an InvalidStateError.\n",
